Cthulhu is meant to be the best, human attempt at pronouncing His name. 
According to Lovecraft to better approximate the pronunciation one has to 
do a gutteral cough followed by KHLOO-loo.

Personally that makes it sound like a fourth grader saying 
"coughbullshitcough" when zinging one of their friends.

According to Chaosium the pronunciation is "kuh-THOO-loo".

I think it would be neat to see something of Lovecraft make its way into 
Nethack except I believe none of his works have fallen into the public 
domain. That is a Good Thing (tm) overall but limits creativity. That's why 
D&D's original deities book from first edition is rare because they used 
Lovecraft's mythos without permission.

